# Labelled prompts for `switchboard guardrails calibrate`.
#
# HONESTY NOTE, and please read it before quoting any number this file
# produces. These 70 prompts were written by hand by the author of this
# project. They are NOT a random sample of anybody's real traffic, and a
# detector measured on prompts written by the person who wrote its rules will
# always look better than it is. Treat the resulting numbers as a smoke test -
# "does this catch obvious cases without tripping over obvious work?" - and
# not as evidence of how it will behave on your team.
#
# The right calibration set is your own. Turn shadow-style flagging on, run it
# for a week, export the flagged requests, and label them yourself.
#
# One JSON object per line. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
